     F*
     F* RPG/400 file description specifications: program described and
     F* externally described files, every device, and continuation lines.
     F*
     F* Member: RPGFIL   Compilable: no (declarations only, no cycle)
     F* Source: RPG/400 Reference SC09-1817, chapter 5 (Tables 12, 16, 17).
     F* Retrieved: 2026-07-26
     F*
     F* 15 type  16 designation  17 end of file  18 sequence
     F* 19 format  24-27 record length  28 limits  29-30 key length
     F* 31 address type  32 organization  33-34 overflow indicator
     F* 35-38 key start  39 extension code  40-46 device
     F* 53 continuation  66 file addition  71-72 file condition
     F* 75-80 comments, shown here in lower case
     F*  1         2         3         4         5         6         7         8
     F*8901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890
     F*
     F* Position 6 of a compiler directive repeats the specification
     F* letter it sits among, which keeps the listing from spacing.
     F/SPACE 1
     F/EJECT
     F*
     F* Externally described files (E in position 19).
     FCUSTMASTIF  E           K        DISK
     FORDDTL  UF  E           K        DISK                      A
     FCUSTDSP CF  E                    WORKSTN
     FINVRPT  O   E                    PRINTER
     F*
     F* Program described files (F in position 19).
     FORDHDR  IPEAF     256  8AI     1 DISK
     FORDSEC  IS  F     128  5PI    17 DISK
     FQSYSPRT O   F     132     OV     PRINTER
     FOVFRPT  O   F     132     OA     PRINTER
     FTAPEOUT O   F      80            SEQ
     F*
     F* Limits processing by a record address file, and the record
     F* address file itself (R in position 16).
     FPARTMASTIF  F     200L10AI     1 DISK
     FPARTRAF IR  F      10   A        DISK
     F*
     F* Extension code E names an array or table file, L names a
     F* line counter specification.
     FTAXTBL  IT  F      10           EDISK
     FRPTFILE O   F     132           LPRINTER
     F*
     F* A SPECIAL device names its own routine in positions 54-59.
     FSPCLIN  IF  F      80            SPECIAL       SPCRTN
     F*
     F* File addition (66), file condition (71-72), comment (75-80).
     FAUDITLOGOF  E                    DISK                      A    U1  audit
     FARCHIVE IF  E           K        DISK                           UC
     FTESTFILEIF  E           K        DISK                           U8
     F*
     F* Continuation lines carry K in position 53. The option goes in
     F* 54-59 and its argument in 60-67.
     FCUSTDSP CF  E                    WORKSTN
     F                                              KINFDS DSPFDS
     F                                              KINFSR *PSSR
     F                                              KNUM          4
     F                                              KID    DEVICE
     F                                              KIND         99
     F                                              KSAVDS SAVEDS
     F                                              KPASS  *NOIND
     F                                              KSLN   STRLIN
     F                                        SFLRRNKSFILE SFLREC
     F            ORDERHDR                          KRENAMEORDHDRR
     F            ORDERTRL                          KIGNORE
     F                                              KPLIST SPCPLST
     FINVMAST UF  E           K        DISK
     F                                              KCOMIT                commit
     F                                              KRECNO RRN
     FRPTPRT  O   F     132            PRINTER
     F                                              KPRTCTLPRTDS
     F*
     F* An option using only 54-65 may sit on the main line itself.
     FJRNFILE UF  E           K        DISK         KCOMIT
     F*
     F* A page and line number in 1-5 does not disturb the columns.
02010FSEQFILE IF  E           K        DISK                               seq
02020F                                              KINFDS SEQFDS         seq
     F*
     F* File translation records, which come after the program with
     F* the other compile-time data. *EQUATE occupies positions 1-7
     F* and position 8 is blank; the first record names the files and
     F* the ones after it give the character pairs, each as two
     F* hexadecimal values.
**
*EQUATE SEQFILE,PRINTER
*EQUATE 5B4A
*EQUATE 7B7C
